        <!-- NOT suppressed, and the reason is a trap this PR walked into.
             Psalm reads the DOCBLOCK `@return` in preference to the native
             return type, so a `@return string|null` sitting above a `: string`
             signature is not a contradiction psalm reports - it is psalm
             quietly using the docblock and ignoring the signature. That is how
             a mutation test on this file came back green while changing the
             code: only the native type was mutated, psalm never read it, and a
             tool that has not looked is indistinguishable from one that is
             satisfied.
             With this rule on, psalm names the divergence directly:
             "Docblock has incorrect return type 'null|string', should be
             'string'". Measured before un-suppressing it: ZERO
             MismatchingDocblockReturnType findings across all 544 files, so the
             suppression was protecting nothing and cost the next person an
             honest mutation test. -->
        <MismatchingDocblockReturnType errorLevel="error"/>
